# graphify — generated code knowledge graph.
#
# Ignored, not committed, for one concrete reason: the post-commit hook rebuilds
# graph.json in the background AFTER each commit, so tracking it would leave the
# tree dirty immediately after every single commit. It is also a pure build
# artifact — derived entirely from source, rebuilt by `graphify update .` in
# seconds with no API key and no network — so it belongs with .next/ and dist/.
#
# .graphifyignore and .claude/settings.json ARE committed: those are the
# configuration a teammate needs to reproduce the same graph.
graphify-out/

# Operator credential drops. cf_tunnel_info.txt holds a LIVE Cloudflare API
# token with full zone rights over ollasuper.com; it sits at the repo root, so
# a single `git add -A` would publish it to a public remote. Ignored by exact
# name AND by pattern, so the next credential file someone drops here is caught
# too. If a token ever does land in a commit, ignoring it afterwards does not
# help — rotate it in the Cloudflare dashboard.
cf_tunnel_info.txt
open_router_key.txt
google_auth.txt
*_auth*.txt
*.client_secret*.json
*_token*.txt
*_secret*.txt
*_key*.txt
*.credentials.json